{# Google Analytics 4 + Microsoft Clarity.
   Defined once here instead of pasted into every page — which is how
   Clarity ended up missing from all 9 members pages in the hand-written site.
   Set `noClarity: true` in a page's front matter to opt that page out. #}
{# Localhost guard, added Aug 30, 2026. The dev server was firing real GA4 hits:
   10 sessions in the first six weeks of data arrived with referrer
   `localhost:8080`. Every `npx eleventy --serve` session was writing into the
   production property.

   A GA4 Data Filter set to Active would also exclude this (Google: excluded
   data "is never processed and will never be available in Google Analytics or
   BigQuery"). This guard is still the better fix, for two reasons: it stops the
   hit being SENT rather than discarding it after collection, so it costs
   nothing and cannot be silently switched off in a console someone else
   administers; and a GA4 exclude filter is irreversible — the data is gone, not
   flagged — which is a heavier instrument than a dev server deserves. #}
<script>
  window.__tpAnalyticsOff =
    ['localhost', '127.0.0.1', '0.0.0.0', '[::1]'].indexOf(location.hostname) !== -1
    || location.hostname.endsWith('.local');
</script>
<!-- Google tag (gtag.js) -->
<script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id={{ site.analytics.ga4 }}"></script>
<script>
  window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
  function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
  gtag('js', new Date());

  if (!window.__tpAnalyticsOff) {
    gtag('config', '{{ site.analytics.ga4 }}');
  }
</script>
{% if not noClarity %}
<!-- Microsoft Clarity -->
<script type="text/javascript">
    if (!window.__tpAnalyticsOff) {
      (function(c,l,a,r,i,t,y){
          c[a]=c[a]||function(){(c[a].q=c[a].q||[]).push(arguments)};
          t=l.createElement(r);t.async=1;t.src="https://www.clarity.ms/tag/"+i;
          y=l.getElementsByTagName(r)[0];y.parentNode.insertBefore(t,y);
      })(window, document, "clarity", "script", "{{ site.analytics.clarity }}");
    }
</script>
{% endif %}
